      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.1 Internet"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The World Wide Web (WWW) was created by Sir Tim Berners-Lee in 1989 at CERN.",
        "A Web Browser is a client-side software application used to render and display web pages, whereas a Search Engine is a web-based service used to index and search content.",
        "Email communication uses SMTP (Simple Mail Transfer Protocol) for sending messages, and POP3 or IMAP for receiving messages.",
        "A Uniform Resource Locator (URL) serves as the unique global address of a web resource.",
        "HTTPS encrypts communication between the browser and server using SSL/TLS over Port 443."
      ],
      "id": "3i2nk70"
    },
