    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "SMTP is strictly used for SENDING emails, whereas POP3 and IMAP are used for RECEIVING emails.",
        "BCC (Blind Carbon Copy) keeps recipient email addresses hidden from all other message recipients.",
        "HTTPS uses SSL/TLS encryption on Port 443, while unencrypted HTTP operates on Port 80.",
        "Tim Berners-Lee developed the World Wide Web, HTML, HTTP, and the first web browser."
      ],
      "id": "626p0ve"
